  "question": {
    "text": "The distance of the point having position vector <math><mo>-</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math> from the straight line passing through the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and parallel to the vector, <math><mn>6</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>7</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let, the given point be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;hence the position vector of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0187_5e862af6e4c9.png\" style=\"width: 491px; height: 310px;\" /></p><p>We know that the vector joining two points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo></math></p><p>Hence, the vector&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>And,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;is the projection of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;on the given line i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>We know that the projection of a vector&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;on a vector&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mfenced></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#8901;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mfenced></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow></mfenced><msqrt><mn>36</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>61</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;units</p><p>The distance between the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p>Thus, <math><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>110</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;units</p><p>Now, in triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;by Pythagoras theorem, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>110</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>61</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;units.</p>"
  }
}